    "updated_at": "2017-12-13T04:52:05Z",
    "body": "I came across this as well (macOS 10.12, develop build from December 2017).\r\nIt seems to be related to real time memory allocation - increasing ServerOptions' memSize changes the number of synths which make supernova silent. \r\n```\r\n(\r\nServer.supernova;\r\ns.options.memSize = 8192; //gets silent around 400 synths\r\n// s.options.memSize = 16384; // gets silent around 800 synths\r\n// s.options.memSize = 32768; // plays all 1000 synths\r\ns.waitForBoot({\r\n\r\n\tSynthDef(\\sinoscfb, {\r\n\t\targ vol = 1;\r\n\t\tvar sig = SinOscFB.ar([ExpRand(100.0, 6000), ExpRand(100.0, 6000)], MouseX.kr(0, 1));\r\n\t\tOut.ar(0, sig * vol);\r\n\t}).send(s);\r\n\r\n\tfork{\r\n\t\tvar maxsynth = 1000;\r\n\t\t1.wait;  // give the SynthDef some more time\r\n\t\tp = ParGroup.new;\r\n\t\tmaxsynth.do({\r\n\t\t\tSynth(\\sinoscfb, [\\vol, 0.1/maxsynth.sqrt], target: p);\r\n\t\t\t\".\".post;\r\n\t\t\t0.05.wait;\r\n\t\t});\r\n\t\tpostf(\"\\n% synths launched.\\n\", maxsynth);\r\n\t}\r\n})\r\n)\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
