    "body": "@jamshark70 thank you for the in-depth response. Good to know why things are this way.\r\nI haven't tested recently, but when I did a while back, supernova did crash on linux when it ran out of memory when allocating more synths. I think the crash is a valid bug that needs to be addressed (at least modified into the behavior on macOS, i.e. silence). \r\nI would say that it would also be optimal for supernova to at least detect when it runs out of memory and print a message; IMHO silence out of nowhere can be rather puzzling.",
